Dear all,

I am trying to impose a linear orthogonality constraint (i.e., a restricted spatial regression model) within a geostatistical SPDE model so as to avoid spatial confounding. This has been mentioned in a few papers (e.g., Ingebrigtsen, Finn Lindgren, and Steinslandand 2014, Lindgren and Rue 2015), and I know that the general approach is to use extraconstr.int <http://extraconstr.int> = list(A = A, e = e), but is there any documentation that provides guidance for appropriately specifying A and e? In particular, I am having a hard time figuring out the correct way to do so when there are multiple linear predictors and/or more than one replicate of the spatial field.

Best,

-tyler scott

