On Wed, 2015-06-24 at 06:13 -0700, Chiara Forlani wrote:
> Hi all,
>
> I’m using inla to run a Bayesian model on binomial data, where the
> covariate has a non-linear effect.
>
> We assume a RW2 model for the covariate. My problem is that I expect a
> smooth estimate for the posterior mean but sometimes I don’t get a
> smooth one and I can’t figure out why.
>
> I tried many tests and simplified the problem in order to understand,
> so the dataset now contains only 3 columns: Y is the number of
> positives, N is the number of tested subjects and X is the independent
> variable.
>
> Here is the code to generate the sample data, run the model and plot
> the posterior mean.

I the issue is the selection of priors for the RW2. I would suggest to
read

http://www.r-inla.org/examples/tutorials/tutorial-on-option-scale-model

and then use

hyper = list(prec = list(prior = "pc.prec", param = c(U, alpha)))

as described in inla.doc("pc.prec"), together with

f(..., model="rw2", scale.model = TRUE)

Best wishes,
H

